  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration** (`kibana_sample_data_logs`, 14,074 requests)\n- Timestamps run from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03.\n- Response codes: 200 (12,832), 404 (801), 503 (441). The only 5xx code present is 503.\n- Main fields: `response`, `url`, `host`, `geo.dest`, `bytes`, `clientip`, `agent`.\n- Top destination countries: CN, IN, US, ID, BR.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-5c739e5a Web logs overview`** (id `137a8922-5e6c-4693-b049-20c93dfcca21`)\n- Total requests (count)\n- Average response size (average of `bytes`)\n- Requests over time (line chart, ES|QL)\n- Requests by response code (bar chart, ES|QL)\n- Time range: 2026-10-01 to 2026-12-31. I first set it to end on 2026-10-12, which would have hidden most of the data, and then widened it.\n\n**Alert rule: `EFF-5c739e5a 5xx spike`** (id `b2eeaefd-7344-403e-8038-d1a6ebbe99b7`)\n- Type: Elasticsearch query rule (`.es-query`), KQL query `response.keyword : 5*`\n- Condition: count > 10 over the last 5 minutes, checked every 1 minute\n- Enabled. The last execution status is `ok`.\n- It has no action connector, so it records alerts but sends no notifications. Adding one would need a connector I haven't set up.\n\n**Caveat:** the rule evaluates the last 5 minutes relative to the current time (2026-10-12). The sample data is dated outside that window, so it won't fire on this data as it stands. Only 503s count, and the rule would need more than 10 of them in a 5-minute span.",
